# Addressed through the mount point as a regular file, not a device node:
# this is what makes it identical whether uboot.env sits on SD (mmcblk0p1),
# USB (sda1) or NVMe (nvme0n1p1) — the same reason foyer-boot.cmd.in uses
# ${devtype}/${devnum} from the running boot rather than a hardcoded device.
# efi.mount (foyer-fs-layout) mounts the ESP read-write at /efi.
#
# The size here must match CONFIG_ENV_SIZE (foyer-uboot.cfg), mkenvimage's
# -s (foyer-ubootenv_1.0.bb) and foyer_envsize in foyer-boot.cmd.in — all
# four address the same on-disk bytes in the same env-file format.
/efi/uboot.env  0x0000  0x4000
